# cezar runtime directory. Everything below .ai/cezar/ is machine-written
# (run state, worktrees, artifacts, locks, receipts) and changes on every
# run, so it must not fail the format gate. The two files that are versioned
# stay checked: the negation re-includes them. A bare `.ai/cezar/` cannot be
# used here, because gitignore semantics do not allow re-including a file
# whose parent directory is excluded — the `*` form excludes the contents
# while keeping the directory itself eligible for a negation.
# A newly added versioned file below .ai/cezar/ needs its own `!` line.
.ai/cezar/*
!.ai/cezar/config.json
!.ai/cezar/.gitignore
